#---
# purpose: "a construction whose capture type is a union is admitted only by a test that CONTAINS it, never one it merely overlaps"
# oracle: oracle.exs
#---
#
# fz-kdt.167, the witness. `mk/1` is called three ways: twice with a value that
# came out of the mailbox, so the capture is typed `any` and the wrapper stores
# a BOXED word, and twice with a literal, so the capture is typed `int` or
# `float` and the wrapper stores a raw one. `P.run/2` forwards all four, so one
# shared body is chosen by a runtime test on the construction.
#
# The union construction OVERLAPS both narrow arms -- an `any` capture could be
# holding an int, or a float -- but it is INSIDE neither, because the layout a
# capture was stored in belongs to the construction and not to the value that
# happens to sit there. Admitting on overlap therefore hands a boxed capture to
# a body whose capture lane is a raw int: on the interpreter the first line
# answers 12.0 instead of 12, and the native door aborts in
# `fz_closure_get_capture_f64`. Admission is containment.
defmodule P do
  fn twice(f, x), do: f.(f.(x))
  fn run(f, x), do: twice(f, x)
  fn mk(c), do: fn (n) -> n + c end
end

fn main() do
  send(self(), 1)
  send(self(), 0.5)
  a = receive do v -> v end
  b = receive do v -> v end
  dbg(P.run(P.mk(a), 10))
  dbg(P.run(P.mk(b), 10))
  dbg(P.run(P.mk(1), 10))
  dbg(P.run(P.mk(0.5), 10))
end
